{"title":"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_-_Recommended_for_Contest\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 - Recommended for Contest</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(similar_to_solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (similar to solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(The_Long_Way)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (The Long Way)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Pythagorean_Theorem_&amp;_Vieta&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Pythagorean Theorem &amp; Vieta's Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, with each vertex of the smaller square on a side of the larger square. A vertex of the smaller square divides a side of the larger square into two segments, one of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and the other of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4cdd3dbcabe3dc76b806d60b785416afc65f11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,2)--(2,2)--(2,0)--(0,0)--cycle); draw((0,0.3)--(0.3,2)--(2,1.7)--(1.7,0)--cycle); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(-0.1,0.15)); label(&quot;$b$&quot;,(-0.1,1.15));[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb18a59eb286ec18f14647f4337672f9db3251d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{1}5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{2}5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{1}2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\hspace{.05in}1\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\hspace{.05in}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"363\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_-_Recommended_for_Contest\">Solution 1 - Recommended for Contest</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 - Recommended for Contest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total area of the four congruent triangles formed by the squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3221e8c5343a25ade88aa4a4d1f3f46626d73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-4 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the area of one of these triangles is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. The height of one of these triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and the base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Using the formula for area of the triangle, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f07068807fdd6bfab83cd418928ad9204f0a32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab}{2} = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. Multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides to find that the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96602e0cc9ac1c013f4c3f11fd90267c5b60c5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Algebra)\">Solution 2 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, so instead of solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we find a way to get an expression with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By the Triple Perpendicularity Model, all four triangles are congruent.\n</p><p>By the Pythagorean Theorem,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b6266fc0f6cfb0132d08d9045a4609c37f03f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2+b^2} = \\sqrt{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74bcd40e455c9bc381e70c051679b6dc5b0a9fc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2+b^2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a305b1efe7e15acdfe721f005d29f417b8b7078a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2eaa7135f53d134f67771f72fe6d3013d497a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+2ab+b^2 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc8769fe7ed7156658c5e78adeada6c4a9de934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5-2ab} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce128d9b67938ea9c038f07f03d6605bc2569702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-2ab = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b2087794396d0d83ccd8a5f8f1f743b04398f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2ab=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f0951356d721e3270489782b79248e5e3bfd201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc2922f16df9d1668284d686b078c4f4e77f864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"53\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28similar_to_solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(similar_to_solution_2)\">Solution 3 (similar to solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (similar to solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that each side of a square is equal, and each the area of a square can be expressed as the side squared. We can let the outside square with area 5's side be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. We get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/0095c9d5698d1aec88ef08847ad5214fd7c7a61e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. Simplifying this we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822d662d07c2943d264b8af683a3ad1e805adbfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sqrt5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>We can then create the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/15411a74d030c92cc3e1c56ace6a24558db1bc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\sqrt5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Using the same tactic we get that the side length of the inner square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41a816b49f96da72db267f58c20cae07a9bd09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 = 2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can then express this expression as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/6328b9c285f95a7bfa2258da725ed4d4a7cb7927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)^2 - 2ab = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/15411a74d030c92cc3e1c56ace6a24558db1bc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\sqrt5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" /> and substitute it into our current equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/617512d1ad50e9a5d95816f48795cab35f380475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt5)^2 - 2ab = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>We further simplify this to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4108262eb76cc28815de28b1306631017ff52779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc65d963faf7b61ca07c193d3f3bdb0a6770394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\frac {1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"55\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28The_Long_Way.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(The_Long_Way)\">Solution 4 (The Long Way)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (The Long Way)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Visually, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/15411a74d030c92cc3e1c56ace6a24558db1bc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\sqrt5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" /> (1) and we can tell that all the triangles are congruent. That means the long side of all the triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and the short side will always be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Notice that the hypotenuse is the side of the smaller square (2). Using the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/4544b48fafaac4d637ef327fd07816356efca48a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/68077ce91224c5c9895f3dc9b10a0c487d41db76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> (2).\n</p><p>Now we just have a system of equations:\n</p><p>Isolate b in (1) -&gt; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/4977a12358493ab6b01e1e68848abdb6d6bb43fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\sqrt5-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />, and plug it in to (2).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fa1c957fe684b20afc0a32811fa48cefdd20ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+(5-a)^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />, Simplifying should get you to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26c9a0b7f1f0f1f3fff8cac688a8e03110e566f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2-2a\\sqrt5+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Using the quadratic formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e09989cee5e583ba14fae2060253169470f1f513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{2\\sqrt5 \\pm \\sqrt{20-8}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying the squareroots, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a898087604c0a29bc41006e98170996a504e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{\\sqrt5+\\sqrt3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>This yields b to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221b0f5edfb5ff700aedc0aee9680a6c4dedf133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt5-\\sqrt3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"43\" /> via substituting into (1)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55c04308b10d19ec0b847512a0e67672a607f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=\\frac{(\\sqrt5+\\sqrt3)(\\sqrt5-\\sqrt3)}{2*2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"217\" height=\"43\" /> (difference of squares) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0388f1bef076749383c5b60770cb6b6d8c69dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{5-3}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\frac {1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"143\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~RandomMathGuy500\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Pythagorean_Theorem_.26_Vieta.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Pythagorean_Theorem_&amp;_Vieta's_Formula)\">Solution 3 (Pythagorean Theorem &amp; Vieta's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Pythagorean Theorem &amp; Vieta&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed as in solution 3 until you get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26c9a0b7f1f0f1f3fff8cac688a8e03110e566f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2-2a\\sqrt5+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />. The two solutions to this equation will be the long and short side of the triangle we are looking for, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> from the problem statement. Using Vieta's formula, their product is the constant term divided by the quadratic term, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc65d963faf7b61ca07c193d3f3bdb0a6770394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\frac {1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"55\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~nbeaudrot\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=2\">https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=2</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MhxGq1sSA6U\">https://youtu.be/MhxGq1sSA6U</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n